<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-SOUTH AFRICA DECLARE SECOND INNNINGS AT 256-6.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-SOUTH AFRICA DECLARE SECOND INNNINGS AT 256-6.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-01-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa declared their second innings at 256 for six, leaving India to score 427 in a minimum of 118 overs, on the fourth day of the second test in Cape Town on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scores: South Africa 529-7 declared and 256-6, India 359.</p>
